The cart already keys items by customer and product, and the customer service already exposes wishlist details. I'll add the add-from-wishlist path on that existing model and wire it into the wishlist page.
Cart unit tests and the wishlist Jest tests passed. I'll run the new cart integration test next, since it needs Docker.
Signed-in shoppers can add a wishlist item to the cart. The wishlist entry stays in place, and a discontinued product cannot be added.

`POST /storefront/items/from-wishlist` loads the wishlist item from the customer service, checks that it belongs to the signed-in shopper, and rejects unavailable products with “Product is no longer available and cannot be added to the cart.” A new cart line is created with quantity 1, or the existing line’s quantity is increased. The wishlist page shows **Add to Cart** for available products and a disabled **Unavailable** button plus the discontinued explanation otherwise.

No new database migration was added. `cart_item` already has a primary key on `(customer_id, product_id)`. The customer service URL was already configured.

